'''Kuuk Yak''', or the '''snake language''', if translated literally, is an [[language extinction|extinct]] [[Paman languages|Paman language]] which was spoken on the [[Cape York Peninsula]] of [[Queensland]], [[Australia]].

Very little is known about the language, but a small number of people in the settlement [[Pormpuraaw, Queensland|Pormpuraaw]] are able to remember bits of the language. [[Barry Alpher]] is currently trying to collect all these pieces and fragments of information for his [[lexicon]] and [[grammar]] of the language, and in order to understand the genetic classification of the language, which had once been thought to perhaps be a [[dialect]] of the [[Kuuk Thaayorre language]].<ref name="AIATSIS" />

